 "summary": "The new stable-range declarations (indexed product, Dedekind-finiteness, unit form, endomorphism and matrix rings, semisimple rings, Jacobson lifting, semilocal) have no existing counterparts in Mathlib or Tau Ceti, and the proofs reuse the available Wedderburn\u2013Artin, opposite-matrix, lattice-complement and noncommutative Jacobson API. The only overlaps are commutative-only (Mathlib `isUnit_of_sub_one_mem_jacobson`, Tau Ceti `IsCoprime.exists_isUnit_add_mul`, `hasStableRangeLE_one_of_finite_maximalSpectrum`) and cannot replace the new general-ring results.",
